{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_68","type":"agent_message","text":"The sweep found three remaining areas of concern: historical closures are still offered for close again; receipt projections suppress dependency acceptance checks; and multi-member exit gates force an aggregate review even under `never`. I also found that backward ADR links are checked for file existence without reading the target.\n\nArtifact-check and surface-check both exited successfully. Artifact-check used its full-history attribution range and emitted warnings, so I’ll note that limit in the evidence. An additional temporary probe was blocked by the read-only sandbox; those findings rest on the inspected code."}}
