{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_81","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: changes-requested\n\nFour medium-severity blockers remain:\n\n- **N17:** Historical milestone approvals are recognized by closeout, but reached/attention projections still demand receipts.\n- **N18:** Receipt projections suppress dependency acceptance checks.\n- **N19:** Exit gates introduce an undocumented exception to `never` and the two-member threshold.\n- **N20:** Backward Markdown associations do not verify target readability.\n\nThe focused policy tests, `go vet ./...`, artifact-check, and surface-check passed. Additional temporary probes were blocked by the read-only sandbox; findings below cite inspected code. The worktree remains unchanged.\n\nApplied the review workflow and Go, security, documentation, and delivery-evidence rules. Reviewed bundle `rvb-b8d3d91f787510d7` against R1–R7 and D1–D2.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N17\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/roadmaps.go\",\n      \"line\": 66,\n      \"summary\": \"Historical milestones are still reopened by projections. closeoutReviewGate recognizes a pre-adoption milestone approval through milestoneClosedBeforeAdoption (closeout_review_policy.go:376,551), but ReachedMilestones asks only closedByReceipt, which returns false immediately when no receipt exists (closeout_review_policy.go:578-580). The same receipt-only condition appears in milestoneReachedObligations (obligation_projection.go:683) and roadmapReachedApartFrom (roadmaps.go:353). A historically approved milestone under an active roadmap is therefore offered for close again and prevents roadmap-reached suggestions, although closeout-check recognizes its historical contract and does not require a receipt. Use a shared terminal projection that also recognizes verified historical closures; do not backfill receipts. This leaves R7 and the prior historical-state correction incomplete.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N18\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy.go\",\n      \"line\": 591,\n      \"summary\": \"closedByReceipt calls getCloseoutState(ref, false), explicitly suppressing dependency acceptance. Under never with no aggregate review, reviewCheck returns the exemption before bundle verification, and closeoutReceiptStands checks only canonical members and exit-gate text. Consequently a receipt whose predecessor or consumed outcome is now unavailable or nonterminal can still read closed to reached, attention and roadmap-reached projections, while GetCloseoutState(ref) with the bound resolver and repeated CLI close reject it. Dependency edges are evaluated only inside the includeFederated branches of review_closeout.go:2764-2792; their definitions include local after/consumes edges as well as remote dependencies (federated_acceptance.go:573-607). Preserve cycle-safe dependency verification in the shared projection instead of disabling that half of terminal verification.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N19\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy.go\",\n      \"line\": 296,\n      \"summary\": \"Any nonempty exit gate on a multi-member milestone forces its own aggregate review, including under never and when-justified with exactly two canonical members. TestCloseoutReviewPolicyRoundFour explicitly asserts this additional condition. R3, R4 and D1 instead specify the deterministic member threshold and a close without aggregate review when exempt; preserving exit-gate verification is a separate obligation, not an approved additional review-policy predicate. POSE.md:374 also documents the original threshold without this exception. Provide independent exit-gate evidence while honoring the selected review mode, or obtain an explicit spec/decision change for the additional aggregate-review requirement.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N20\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go\",\n      \"line\": 190,\n      \"summary\": \"Backward Markdown targets are checked with Lstat and containment only; they are never read or resolved through GetRoadmap. For example, an inventoried ADR linking to ../roadmaps/other.md whose directory entry is regular but whose content cannot be read produces no diagnostic while evaluating another roadmap. The evaluator can therefore report Known=true and prove absence despite an unreadable local association target. The adjacent roadmaps: declaration path does perform GetRoadmap and detects this condition at line 173. Apply equivalent real target resolution to Markdown links and test ReadFile failure separately from missing-file and symlink cases, as required by R3's association contract.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R1-F1\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"closeout_review_policy.go:322-331 builds the effective plan without recursive closeout gating and checks its composed independence and base profile. Protected overlays are read at the baseline revision at lines 442-452. The focused TestCloseoutReviewPolicy suite passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R1-F2\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"evidence\": \"closeout_review_policy.go:389-409 now verifies canonical members and ExitGateDigest without reevaluating current policy, fixing exit-gate drift and later-policy reinterpretation. SubjectDigest is still not verified and dependency inputs are absent from closeoutSubject:468-507; the resulting projection gap is N18.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R1-F3\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"evidence\": \"closeout_review_policy.go:519-570 adds positive historical approval checks and the pre-adoption sealed-plan marker; the gate uses them at line 376. However reached, attention and roadmap-reached projections still require a receipt for these historical milestones, as reported in N17.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R1-F6\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"evidence\": \"closedByReceipt:577-595 now checks domain terminal state rather than receipt presence or aggregate review alone. Doctor uses it at line 654. Its includeFederated=false call still omits dependency acceptance, leaving N18.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R2-N1\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"closeout_review_policy.go:435 retains adopted baselines even when enabled=false; lines 438-452 restore baseline mandatory-human independence and load baseline base/overlay profiles through parseReviewProfileAt. The focused policy suite passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R3-N9\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"closeout_review_policy.go:316-320 refuses exemption when a missing current kind profile accompanies a review-governance change. Lines 442-452 independently inspect protected baseline overlays, including when the current mapping is absent.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R3-N10\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"evidence\": \"closeout_review_policy.go:296-301 prevents an unjudged multi-member exit gate from being exempted. The replacement forces the full aggregate review under never and below the when-justified threshold, creating the requirements mismatch in N19.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R3-N11\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"review_closeout.go:2830 restricts removeReviewOnlyBlockers to the legacy path where review.CloseoutReview is nil. Adopted exemptions retain child-scope blockers irrespective of names containing review, criterion or finding.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R3-N12\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"evidence\": \"closeout_adr_associations.go:183-196 now diagnoses missing and nonregular backward Markdown targets before comparing paths. It still checks only metadata, not target readability, unlike the frontmatter path at line 173; see N20.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R3-N13\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"evidence\": \"closeout_review_policy.go:591 now invokes getCloseoutState, so child review and lifecycle blockers are checked. The false argument suppresses dependency acceptance, leaving the incomplete terminal projection described in N18.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R3-N14\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"review_closeout.go:2824-2829 reevaluates receipt-backed roadmap cut criteria through roadmapCriteriaBlockers. closeout_receipt.go:267-298 checks criterion results and verifies manual-review references still resolve within the project.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R3-N15\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \".pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:130 declares pose-mcp/internal/pose/spec.go. Both requested strict artifact-check and surface-check commands exited 0; surface-check reported surface.findings=0.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R3-N16\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"evidence\": \"closeout_review_policy.go:551-570 recognizes an approved milestone whose sealed plan has no CloseoutReview, and the RoundFour regression checks ReviewCheck and CloseRequired. The receipt-only readers in roadmaps.go:66,353 and obligation_projection.go:683 still project that historical milestone as requiring close; see N17.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Inspected the supplied range, requirements R1-R7, technical plan, accepted ADR and D1-D2. Accounted for all 13 prior findings. Swept policy parsing/defaults, adoption/setup/update separation, schema-preserving capability toggles, canonical member/redirect resolution, ADR associations in both directions, baseline and mandatory-human protection, voluntary-review vetoes, immutable receipt parsing/publication/intents, historical classification, CLI close/recovery/repeat-close, review-check, bundle verification, review-plan, closeout state/check, reached/nextCloses, attention/obligations, roadmap gates, MCP projections, federation source proof and doctor. Compared documentation/templates/scaffold and schemas with runtime behavior. Examined the adversarial corpus's retained-child and parent-outlives-rejected-child coverage; it does not cover the remaining historical and dependency projection gaps. Ran focused policy tests across domain/CLI/MCP, go vet, artifact-check, surface-check, suggest-review, context resolution, recurrence-check and clean-worktree checks. An additional overlay probe could not create temporary files under the read-only sandbox; findings are source-established, not claimed as reproduced by that probe. No repository changes or attestation were made.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Checked implementer claims against the spec, ADR, current code and focused tests. Distinguished verified command outcomes from source-established defects and the unavailable additional probe. Historical closure requires positive evidence; no hand-edited receipt authenticity or lock-ignoring writer protection was assumed, and no residual risk is accepted.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected protected publication, input rechecks, ExpectAbsent receipts and status/intent/receipt ordering. No new goroutine lifecycle was introduced; existing guarded publication machinery is reused.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N17\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Historical terminal-state projections do not preserve the promised migration contract consistently.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N20\",\n      \"rationale\": \"An unreadable backward association target does not become an unknown diagnostic.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N18\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reached/attention projections omit acceptance checks that authoritative closeout and CLI gates perform.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/typed-diagnostics-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected unknown-member diagnostics, receipt corruption/drift errors, close publication/recovery messages and doctor explanations. Returned context identifies the affected scope and remediation without introducing sensitive logging. Incorrect projection behavior is separately reported.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N17\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Schema 5 explicitly rejects older engines and preserves optional reference/transfer adoption, but historical milestone closure remains inconsistent across readers.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N18\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Receipt-backed projections can claim closure without checking applicable dependency acceptance.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N19\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The shared evaluator, explicit adoption and separate receipt address the stated cost and lifecycle causes. The extra exit-gate predicate changes the approved deterministic review rule without a corresponding decision.\",\n      \"mappings\": [\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-607ff681\",\n          \"basis\": \"D2\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The roadmap template's adrs field supplies the explicit local ADR association metadata selected by D2 to implement R3.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-ec2d86f4\",\n          \"basis\": \"R1\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The added accepted ADR records the required policy location, three modes, default, deterministic thresholds and historical compatibility decision.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N19\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The manuals describe the approved member threshold but omit the runtime's additional aggregate-review requirement for multi-member exit gates.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N17\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Operators receive close instructions for historical milestones whose authoritative verifier requires no receipt, and roadmap-reached suggestions can be suppressed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N19\",\n      \"rationale\": \"R3 and R4's exempt-close behavior is not implemented for multi-member milestones with exit gates; R7 and unknown-association requirements also have the reported gaps.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N19\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The implementation footprint follows the declared scope, but the additional aggregate-review predicate extends the approved semantics.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected canonical project identity, verified redirects, confined ADR/receipt paths, strict receipt parsing, baseline protection, mandatory-human handling and recorded-review vetoes. Authoritative federation source proof calls GetCloseoutState before accepting a receipt. No new credentials or authority-write surface was introduced. N18 concerns derived projections and remains blocking under correctness/integration.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N19\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reusing catalog/adopt/setup and domain receipt publication is proportionate; global ADR identity and remote backlink discovery are correctly excluded. Requiring a complete aggregate review merely to judge an otherwise exempt exit gate exceeds the selected cost rule. Separate gate evidence is the smaller sufficient alternative; an explicit approved exception would change that assessment.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed and exited 0. Output reported artifact.claims=40, artifact.observed=83 and artifact.findings=925, with warnings. Automatic attribution selected full-history change set cs-d9f7f840bced ending at 0e54c85a0ce2cb1728c454c74c2b66e7ca95c49e, beyond this bundle's sealed head; this command outcome is not represented as exact-range reconciliation. The supplied range was inspected separately.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-c37beb4b1497724a\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Did not run a state-writing assessment in the read-only review. Examined the sealed structural evidence and mapped both list